277:            <p className="leading-[22.5px] whitespace-pre-wrap">Unlike traditional e-commerce, rewards users don’t visit with a specific product in mind. Infrequent visits to spend accumulated points make exploration more important than search.</p>
292:            <p className="leading-[22.5px] whitespace-pre-wrap">Infrequent visits weaken product awareness</p>
295:            <p className="leading-[22.5px] whitespace-pre-wrap">Because users don’t visit often, they don’t have a clear sense of what the store offers. Over time, it becomes hard to understand the full breadth of rewards.</p>
310:            <p className="leading-[22.5px] whitespace-pre-wrap">Search fails without prior discovery</p>
313:            <p className="leading-[22.5px] whitespace-pre-wrap">Search only works once users know what exists. Without upfront visibility into available options, users don’t know what to search for and disengage early.</p>
